ays see a Beetles coming, remember.", "reference": "2006, Michael J. Flores, Deckade: 10 Years of Decks, Thoughts, and Theory!, →ISBN, page 235:"}, {"text": "When a player does discard or use a card or when a creature also died or a spell gets destroyed, that card gets placed into the player's graveyard.", "reference": "2015, Kinetik Gaming, Magic the Gathering Game Guide (Unofficial), →ISBN:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(sports) A team where players are sent when they are not useful, or a team where players become useless if sent there.", "tags": ["broadly", "figuratively"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}]}, {"definition": "(attributively) A period very early in the morning in which there is very little activity.", "tags": ["attributive"], "examples": ["graveyard shift, graveyard slot, graveyard watch"], "quotes": [{"text": "Her husband, of course, came dressed as Herman Melville.) She's a veteran of these marathons, and warned me about the forthcoming graveyard stretch—when Moby-Dick melds with the altered brain chemistry of sleep deprivation.", "reference": "2024 January 14, Luke Winkie, “A Whale of a Time”, in Slate, New York, N.Y.: The Slate Group, →ISSN, →OCLC, archived from the original on 17 Jan 2024:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(US, slang) Synonym of suicide (“beverage combining all available flavors at a soda fountain”).", "tags": ["US", "slang"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["suicide"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graveyard", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}